    "body": "## Motivation\n\nCookbook benchmark cards for non-GPU hardware call the accelerator a GPU. For example, [GLM-5.3-Flash on TPU7x](https://lmsysorg.mintlify.app/cookbook/autoregressive/GLM/GLM-5.3-Flash#hw=tpu7x&strategy=low-latency&quant=fp8&pdMode=unified&kvDsaPair=fp8-pallas&bcg=off&mmTransport=auto&hicache=off&parsers=auto) shows \"throughput per gpu\". The label is hardcoded in the shared engine, so every TPU, Ascend NPU, CPU, and Apple Silicon card has the same problem.\n\n## Modifications\n\n`docs/src/snippets/_deployment.jsx`:\n\n- Move `vendorOf` from inside the docker-command builder up to component scope, next to `HARDWARE_CATALOG`, so the benchmark card can use it. The function body is unchanged.\n- Add `deviceUnitOf(hwId)`. It returns `\"chip\"` for the `tpu`, `npu`, `cpu`, and `apple` vendors and `\"gpu\"` for everything else.\n- Build the Speed table's throughput row label and its legend from that unit. GPU hardware still shows `throughput per gpu ... /elapsed/GPU`. TPU and other non-GPU hardware now show `throughput per chip ... /elapsed/chip`.\n\nThe `tokens_per_sec_per_gpu` data key is unchanged, so no benchmark files need edits.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `node docs/scripts/check_cookbook_configs.mjs`: `cookbook config check: OK`\n- `node --test docs/scripts/tests/*.test.mjs`: 52/52 pass\n- I have not rendered the page with `mint dev`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:white_check_mark: [Run #40175191223](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40175191223)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40175191251](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40175191251)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:heavy_minus_sign: **No AMD PR run found for this commit**.<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n